  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the rectangle bordered by a repeated number\n    # Look for a rectangular border pattern\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            # Check if this could be top-left of a border\n            # Find horizontal run\n            c_end = c\n            while c_end < cols and grid[r][c_end] == val:\n                c_end += 1\n            width = c_end - c\n            if width < 3:\n                continue\n            # Check if there's a matching bottom border\n            for r_end in range(r + 2, rows):\n                # Check bottom border\n                if all(grid[r_end][c + i] == val for i in range(width)):\n                    # Check left and right columns\n                    if all(grid[r + i][c] == val and grid[r + i][c + width - 1] == val for i in range(r_end - r + 1)):\n                        # Extract interior\n                        result = []\n                        for ri in range(r + 1, r_end):\n                            row = []\n                            for ci in range(c + 1, c + width - 1):\n                                row.append(grid[ri][ci])\n                            result.append(row)\n                        return result\n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find the rectangle bordered by a repeated number\n    # Look for a rectangular border pattern\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            # Check if this could be top-left of a border\n            # Find horizontal run\n            c_end = c\n            while c_end < cols and grid[r][c_end] == val:\n                c_end += 1\n            width = c_end - c\n            if width < 3:\n                continue\n            # Check if there's a matching bottom border\n            for r_end in range(r + 2, rows):\n                # Check bottom border\n                if all(grid[r_end][c + i] == val for i in range(width)):\n                    # Check left and right columns\n                    if all(grid[r + i][c] == val and grid[r + i][c + width - 1] == val for i in range(r_end - r + 1)):\n                        # Extract interior\n                        result = []\n                        for ri in range(r + 1, r_end):\n                            row = []\n                            for ci in range(c + 1, c + width - 1):\n                                row.append(grid[ri][ci])\n                            result.append(row)\n                        return result\n    return grid",
